%% sequence-diagram.mmd — one call turn across service boundaries
%% Source for docs/architecture.md's turn-by-turn walkthrough.
%% Render with: mmdc -i sequence-diagram.mmd -o sequence-diagram.png
%% Includes all 12 services. An earlier draft had 16 -- tool-gateway,
%% sentiment-detector, model-router, and inference-router were folded into
%% compliance/llm-gateway/infrastructure after none of the four cleared this
%% design's own criteria for a standalone service. See docs/architecture.md's
%% "Consolidated into an existing service, not left as a separate one".

sequenceDiagram
    participant Borrower
    participant Media as Media Server
    participant VAD as vad-service
    participant DNS as denoiser
    participant STT as stt-service
    participant ORCH as call-orchestrator
    participant LLM as llm-gateway
    participant COMP as compliance
    participant RAG as rag-service
    participant SESS as session-manager
    participant TTS as tts-service

    Borrower->>Media: RTP audio
    Media->>VAD: raw frame
    VAD->>VAD: hangover-window end-of-speech check
    VAD-->>DNS: speech frames only (silence dropped)
    DNS-->>STT: denoised audio
    STT-->>ORCH: transcript (partial, then final)
    ORCH->>SESS: GET current call state
    SESS-->>ORCH: state, slots

    ORCH->>LLM: classify(text, audio)
    Note over LLM: Internally: picks small/large model tier,<br/>classifies intent, classifies sentiment from<br/>tone — folded-in responsibilities, not separate<br/>network hops. See services/llm-gateway/main.py.
    LLM-->>ORCH: intent, sentiment

    ORCH->>COMP: transition(current_state, intent, sentiment)

    opt intent = faq_or_policy_question
        COMP->>RAG: retrieve(query, account_context)
        RAG-->>COMP: passages, confident_match
    end

    Note over COMP: If the transition needs an external fact or<br/>action (e.g. balance, schedule payment): invokes<br/>a registered tool internally against the loan<br/>servicing backend/CRM — folded in, not a separate<br/>network hop. See services/compliance/main.py.

    COMP-->>ORCH: next_state, response_text, should_escalate
    ORCH->>SESS: PATCH state, transcript_entry
    ORCH->>TTS: synthesize/stream(response_text)
    TTS-->>Media: audio chunks (streamed)
    Media-->>Borrower: bot speech

    Note over VAD,TTS: If VAD detects speech onset while<br/>TTS is still streaming: barge-in —<br/>orchestrator stops reading the TTS<br/>stream and processes the new utterance.
    Note over STT,TTS: stt-service, llm-gateway, and tts-service all sit<br/>behind a shared GPU batching/load-balancing layer<br/>(Triton or vLLM/TensorRT-LLM's own serving stack —<br/>infrastructure, not a service) — omitted as a<br/>per-call hop here for readability; see<br/>deployment-diagram.mmd for where it sits.
